# Aqara M1S Local Radio — Media Player Connection and Automatic Audio Process Cleanup

## Purpose

This document covers two components:

1. playing an internet radio stream from Home Assistant through:

```text
media_player.aqara_m1s_local_radio
```

2. automatically cleaning suspended audio processes directly on the Aqara M1S hub, specifically stale `nc` listeners on port `12346`.

The observed issue is that Home Assistant may continue to display the media player as `playing`, while the hub is no longer producing audio. The identified cause was an accumulation of suspended processes such as:

```text
nc -l -p 12346
```

In the hub process list, these processes appear with state `T`.

---

# Audio Connection Architecture

The radio path is:

```text
Home Assistant
    |
    | media_player.play_media
    v
media_player.aqara_m1s_local_radio
    |
    | audio stream processed by the local integration
    v
TCP connection to the Aqara M1S hub on port 12346
    |
    v
nc -l -p 12346
    |
    v
aplay -t raw -f S32_LE -c 1 -r 32000
    |
    v
Aqara M1S audio output
```

The Home Assistant entity controls the logical playback state, but the actual audio output depends on the local `nc` and `aplay` processes running on the hub.

If one of these processes becomes suspended or stale, the entity may remain in the `playing` state even though no sound is produced.

---

# Media Player Entity

The media player entity used by this setup is:

```text
media_player.aqara_m1s_local_radio
```

Example: start radio playback directly:

```yaml
action: media_player.play_media
target:
  entity_id: media_player.aqara_m1s_local_radio
data:
  media_content_id: "https://live.radiocafe.ro:8443/live.aac"
  media_content_type: music
```

Example: stop playback:

```yaml
action: media_player.media_stop
target:
  entity_id: media_player.aqara_m1s_local_radio
```

